us="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKIAGE, NORIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKYO ELECTRON LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKIAGE NORIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKIAGE, NORIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method comprising: a plasma-generating step in which a film-forming gas comprising a carbone/fluorine compound and an etching gas for etching a fluorine-containing carbon film are converted to a plasma; and a film deposition step in which a fluorine-containing carbon film is formed on a work from the plasma. The film-forming gas may contain, for example, a gas of a compound having a benzene ring. An example of the etching gas is a gas comprising fluorine. Thus, recessed parts can be satisfactorily filled up.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Le procédé de l'invention commence par une opération de génération de plasma par laquelle on convertit en plasma d'une part un gaz filmogène comprenant un composé fluoro-carboné, et d'autre part un gaz d'attaque chimique permettant d'attaquer chimiquement un film organique fluoré. Le gaz filmogène peut comporter notamment un composé gazeux portant un cycle benzène. Le gaz d'attaque chimique peut être notamment un gaz fluoré. Le procédé permet de combler de façon satisfaisante les zones en creux.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but